msgid "I will set it down for you. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "May I have another potion? "
msgctxt "bark 0421:8E1A"
msgid "Nay, my friend, I have not had the time to concoct another. Perhaps it will be ready for your next visit. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I wish to buy reagents. " or "I wish to buy more reagents. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:8ED8"
msgid "Very well. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I wish to learn spells. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:8F4C"
msgid "You wish to learn spells from me? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I wish to learn spells. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:8FB3"
msgid "Perhaps in the future I will have the time to show you. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I want to recreate the obelisk. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:921A"
msgid "Recreate the obelisk? Do you mean that you wish reconstruct the Blackrock obelisk of the Great Temple? Of course! You are hoping to use the conduit as a way to leave Pagan! I know just the spell you will need. You must cast the Ethereal Travel spell. I do not know where the spell will send you on your first attempt, though I expect the Titans will intervene and direct your journey. Should you encounter and defeat them, know that you would have the worship and admiration of all Pagans. Good luck... "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Things are well. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:92B8"
msgid "I am very glad to hear that. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Things are well. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:939F"
msgid "By the way, considering the tumultuous effect you have had on Pagan, may I commend you on your ability to rouse, or should I say anger, the Titans. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Things are well. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:94C0"
msgid "By the way, I hope you realize the effect of taking the Breath of Wind. The citizens have little in the way of healing now. Please understand that I do not disagree with your choice of action, but I wanted to be sure you are cognizant of the ramifications. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Things are well. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:9562"
msgid "By the way, I notice your presence carries with it a tremendous impact, so to speak. I assume the quakes are your responsibility. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Things are well. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:95AE"
msgid "Is there perhaps something you wish to discuss? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "No. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:9646"
msgid "Very well, then, I shall return to my work. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Yes. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:96AB"
msgid "Very well, then, and what would that be? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I found this with the Sorcerers. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:9743"
msgid "That piece of black stone? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I found this with the Sorcerers. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:9825"
msgid "It is not obsidian, that much is obvious. I wonder if it could be... You say it came from the Sorcerers, eh? It is possible you have found one of the Fragments of the obelisk in the Ancient Temple. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I found this with the Sorcerers. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:98F8"
msgid "Somewhere I have a book that might delve into greater detail. You're welcome to it if you can find it. I would strongly suggest that you study it closely before we continue our discussion. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Goodbye. "
#. sentence template: keep the {placeholders}
msgctxt "bark 0421:99F0"
msgid "Farewell and good luck, {name}."
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Goodbye. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:9CB2"
msgid "Wait. Before you go, my friend, I wish to give you two items that I believe will assist you in your travels. The first is an item of recall I acquire many years ago. When you find yourself in trouble, you may use this item to teleport to my front door. How powerful this item is, I cannot say, for I do not know whether other, stronger powers may prevent it from functioning at certain times.~Furthermore, I wish to give you this potion of healing, which will magically aid the recovery of your wounds. I will try to have others for you as you make return visits, but since the cost to me in time and energy is great, I will not have one for you every time you visit me."
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Goodbye. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:9D2F"
msgid "Excellent. Use this well. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Goodbye. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:9D61"
msgid "Here. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Goodbye. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:9DAD"
msgid "I will set it down for you. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Goodbye. "
msgctxt "bark 0421:9DD7"
msgid "Again, fare well. "
msgstr ""

#. event 11 (leaveFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 0421:9F42"
msgid "I do not wish to do this. "
msgstr ""

#. event 11 (leaveFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 0421:9F6C"
msgid "Kal Vas Grav Corp!"
msgstr ""

#. event 11 (leaveFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 0421:A115"
msgid "A pity... "
msgstr ""
